/* Beat 5, composed onto ScreenScaffold. The one screen that consumes
 * creatures, so the destruction notice is a coral panel rather than a
 * coloured line - splice_confirm_spec 4 wants the consequence unmissable -
 * and it is the LAST child of the content region, directly above the CTA,
 * which is section 3's own requirement.
 *
 * NINE RULES' WORTH OF TREATMENT LEFT THIS FILE IN PHASE 8 TASK 10 AND NONE
 * WAS REPLACED BY A COPY HERE, which is the test of whether a screen composes
 * the layer or re-derives it:
 *   - the root's `padding: var(--gutter)` is the scaffold's content region.
 *   - the destruction notice, the coverage warning and the mutation line each
 *     restated a fill, a radius and --space-2/3 of padding that are exactly
 *     Theme's `.panel-coral`, `.panel-amber` and `.panel-violet`, plus an ink
 *     that is exactly `.t-danger`, `.t-warn` and `.t-violet`. Twelve
 *     declarations, three components, one vocabulary.
 *   - `__forecast`'s surface, card radius, divider border and --space-3
 *     padding were a re-derivation of `SectionCard`, which now draws it - and
 *     which also brings the elevation the hand-rolled version never had.
 *   - `.forecast-row`'s own font-size is `StatCell`'s `t-micro`/`t-num` pair.
 *     That swap is the point of the change rather than a side effect: see
 *     SpliceChamberView.ForecastCellFor.
 *   - `__cta`'s top margin is the CTA row's padding, and its whole treatment
 *     is Theme's `.btn-primary`.
 *
 * WHAT IS LEFT IS THE FOUR THINGS NEITHER THE FRAME NOR A COMPONENT KNOWS:
 * that the parents sit side by side, that a locked-out one is dimmed, that
 * the forecast cells sit in a row, and that three of these labels wrap.
 */
.splice-chamber-view { flex-grow: 1; }

.splice-chamber-view__parents { flex-direction: row; justify-content: space-between; }

/* A Founder the player already named is visibly out of reach, not hidden -
 * bible 3.3's rule read from the splice side. */
.splice-chamber-view__parents > .creature-card.locked-out { opacity: 0.4; }

/* THE HANDOFF'S THREE-CELL STAT ROW, AND THREE IS THE ACTUAL CEILING RATHER
 * THAN A HOPE. `combatPool` (services/api/src/splice/distribution.ts) is the
 * two parents' four combat slots; `merged()` drops every entry carrying the
 * locked trait and then collapses duplicate (trait, tier) pairs, so `combat2`
 * can hold at most three distinct outcomes and usually holds two. A row of
 * `flex-basis: 0` cells therefore never gets narrower than a third of the
 * card, which is what makes the row safe where an unbounded list would not
 * be. */
.splice-chamber-view__forecast { flex-direction: row; }

/* The empty case is one element in a row of cells, so it has to be told to
 * take the whole line - a StatCell grows because StatCell.uss says so, and
 * nothing says it for an EmptyState. */
.splice-chamber-view__forecast > .empty-state { flex-grow: 1; }

/* Three sentences, not labels, so they wrap. The coverage warning also
 * COLLAPSES when the server named nothing - SpliceChamberView.Bind has the
 * measurement. */
.splice-chamber-view__mutation { white-space: normal; margin-top: var(--space-2); }
.splice-chamber-view__coverage-warning { white-space: normal; margin-top: var(--space-2); }
.splice-chamber-view__destruction-notice { white-space: normal; margin-top: var(--space-3); }
